  Linux doesn't run on Turbo Channel Alpha's yet, so you can't install
linux on it.  Try NetBSD, or attack porting linux to the 3000.  I know
that aboot has been ported, but the real time clock is causing a kernel
crash, look at
http://www.phys.ufl.edu/~prescott/linux/alpha/dec3000-port.html for the
current status.  
  Your other option is the $99 hobbist license for Tru64 unix, which
runs very well on the 3000's and is the only way to get full use of all
the hardware.  (The box does have on-board ISDN but it only works under
Tru64)
