>   the init stop at alphabios loading,"no hard drive found on lsi scsi
> adapter"

What do you have the jumpers for SCSI ID set to on each of the disks?
Duplicate IDs can cause strange problems like no drives detected.

Are you properly terminated?  I recently learned the hard way, that LVD
drives
have NO termination onboard, thus requiring active termination on the
SCSI cable.  So, if you have 2 [ or more ] disks, you should have a
setup that looks something like this:

                           Wide SCSI-2 cable
          +---------------+---------------+---------------+---... unused
cable
          |               | ID 0          | ID 1          |        with
more
     +----+------+    +---+---+       +---+---+         Active     
connectors
     |HostAdapter|    | LVD HD|       | LVD HD|       Terminator
     +----######-+    +-------+       +-------+



Have you done this?

