Kjoe (h.vanbrug@syntegra.nl) wrote:
: it didnt work.. i got a double stop error this time.. any clues as to what
: makes the custom kernels fail? is it the RTC? 

Could be.  Usually this is a setup for interrupt structures.  Anything
which has to do with IDE is a more likely candidate.  I do not know
quirks of your hardware so I am not sure.

The general idea in cases like yours is to simplify your configuration
to a bare minimum required to boot and, if succesful, add extra features
until something will break. :-)  Normally a short experimentation 
reveals a culprit but it helps to have another working Alpha around when
doing that. :-)
  
: and my harddisk still isnt bootable.. 

??? That means what?

: on intel systems its easy, install lilo but somehow SRM from alpha
: doesnt find my default installed redhat harddisk (/dev/sda1) not
