It is actually much easier do that on Alphas - even with ARC and not
mentioning SRM.  You do not have to deal with all kind of broken
in a concept BIOSes with weird ideas.

: how do i make that so..

You write a bootblock on your disk with a help of /sbin/swriteboot
and that is about it for now and for the future.  Optionally you
can use 'abootconf' to mark on which partition to look for your
/etc/aboot.conf - but this is not required if convenient.  Documentation
in /usr/doc/aboot-... is not that bad, if you bother to look at it,
even if in places it can use some updates.

