Kernel is important, but the most important thing to watch out
for Alpha executables is  - which compiler was used ?? I vaguely
remeber that distributed.net Alpha client was not compiled using
the best compiler available for Alpha - Compaq C.

Generally speaking, you need to realize that Alpha and Pentium
are *different* chips :-) and so what matters a lot is if their
specific strong points (e.g. available instructions such as MVI
for our SX) were used during implementation of that particular
algorithm or not. There are many compilers out here which are
optimized to take into account only Pentium's specific details
and almost ignore the rest of CPUs.

Besides, the Alpha is better in fp. Crypto applications are almost
100% integer applications, where the difference comparing with
other CPUs is smaller.

Another issue to consider is - if Alpha's 64-bitness (registers) is
used in dnetc client or not.
