I don't have a good answer to your question but have a few related
comments.  Under Tru64 many programs benefit from the -O5 optimization
flag.  -O corresponds to -O4 so at least you're running close to
the best optimization level.  Also, I've seen improvement with
some codes by adding "-speculate all" and "-fast" flags.

Also, I had a DP21264 500MHz NT box at one time.  Its performance was
horrible.  I could never figure out why it was such a dog, but it was
nowhere near as fast as other people's Tru64 21264 Alphas.

