Mathieu Millet <llihtam@minet.net> writes:

> So, My questions are how can I mount my CD reader and how can I force
> the kernel to use Ultra Wide not Fast-Wide ?
> As I'm not really scsi-aware, there may be a problem with the parameters
> of my scsi card for the CDs which could interfere under linux with the
> HD, since 20 MBytes/s = UltraNarrow = Fast-Wide.

Well first of all if you mix SCSI devices you will always be forced to
use the lowest denominator. That is if you mix fast-SCSI and
Ultra-SCSI your machine will be using fast-SCSI on all
devices. Secondly you have to be aware not to mix single ended and
differential (doesn't look like it in your case).

In your case you should either put wour fast HD's on a second
controller or let all devices use the slowest speed (8 bit 50pin).

To get to know more take a look at:
http://www.scsifaq.org/

-- 
Sven Esbjerg



