> What processor is in this?  Except for the DEC part of the name it sounds
> like you're refering to a VAX 4000.  If that's the case I don't believe
> Linux has been ported, however, NetBSD might run on the system.
> 
>                         Zane

   The box you have is a DEC 4000 aka: Cobra, first generation Alpha based on
the 21064 processor. Up to two CPUs, Futurebus+ I/O, and internal SCSI disks.
Futurebus+ was a marketing flop as there was never much third-party device
support, and in the transition to PCI, DEC prematurely cancelled all of the
internally designed Futurebus+ cards. It left a gaping hole in the product 
line for quite a while until the PCI bus machines appeared.

   The Futurebus+/XMI based machines never ran Linux as the drivers were
never written for the I/O architecture.

