Steve Lionel wrote:

> I do think that the suggestion to
> build a statically linked image on Tru64 and running it as a test on
> Linux will produce useful data. (I am obligated to note that,
> technically, doing this violates the terms of your Tru64 UNIX license
> agreement, since it means you will be running OSF-licensed code (from
> the Tru64 UNIX libraries) on a system not covered by a license from
> OSF.)

And I am obliged to point out that this can only be true if and only if
you bought the machine *without* an OSF license to begin with.

I am still convinced, even given the (for Europeans) incomprehensible US
law on these matters, it is the case that if you buy two Alpha systems,
both with a Tru64 UNIX license, and - afterwards - you decide to use one
of them under Linux, you're *still* allowed to _run_ the executables you
produce on the machine running Tru64, on the machine running Linux.

But, IANAL.

