I recently slapped a Sound Blaster AWE64 into my 164lx and I'm having
some trouble getting it set up just right.

I followed the Sound-HOWTO and the Sound Blaster AWE 32/64 HOWTO.  My
kernel seems to be compiled properly, however I'm having trouble with my
/etc/isapnp.conf

When I cold boot the machine (after a shutdown -h) sound doesn't work. 
I get errors while it's setting up the ISA PnP devices.  It complains
when setting up "LD 2" and recommends adding "(VERIFYLD N)"  to my
script to fix it.  If I add this line the error messages no longer
appear, but sound still doesn't work.

HOWEVER, if I warm boot the machine (after a shutdown -r) sound DOES
work.  I do get an error message saying "resource conflict allocating
IRQ 5", but sound does work.

Does anyone know why this is happening?  What I can do to fix it?  What
the correct /etc/isapnp.conf is?

Thanks,

Bill Welch

