Anthony wrote:

> How do I install RH 6.2 alpha.  SO far all I managed to figure out is how to
> get a milo prompt.  Now what?

Booting from CD doesn't work on all systems ,so I suggest you to rawrite root &
ramdisks.
When you have created those disks ,insert root disket and type "boot
fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1"

So ,milo boots kernel named vmlinux.gz from floppy ,then it looks that root fs
is in floppy and ramdisk must be loaded.





