I just picked up a Multia at the MIT flea too.  I saw only the one there,
maybe you got there earlier than I did.  ;-)  Neat little box!

I solved the dead battery problem without buying that overpriced 4.5V 
battery or waiting for shipping.  Make your own battery by soldering
together three 1.5V cells.

I used N cells, but you could just as easily use AAA or even AA if you
think they will fit.  Solder them together in series making a nice little
three battery stack.  Cut the wire pigtail off the old battery and re-use
it.  Peel the Velcro off the old battery and stick it to the bottom of
your little battery stack.  Plug it in and go.  Cost < $6.
