Tom Crabtree (tccrab@sunset.net) wrote:

: Double check the SCSI ID's.

I found the problem last night by connecting the disk to a Linux PC with a
SCSI card and booting it, and yes, it was ID related.  The disk was trying
to claim ALL SCSI IDs!

I watched as detected hardware scrolled by and as that disk gobbled up all
the IDs.  Linux assigned it to /dev/sda sdb, sdc, sdd, and so on.  Turns
out that the SCSI ID selector on the box was wired backwards and all the
ID selector pins were grounded together.

After undoing this, the disk is behaving very well and the Multia is now
running RH 6.1 on it.

Thanks for the advice.
-- 
