Almost....
    On the Alpha, the unaligned trap is a "informational message" to let you
know that data was accessed which was on a byte boundary instead of a word
boundary. The Alpha has to manipulate "byte" boundary data using firmware
routines which slow it down.  messages are a pain but do not indicate an
error.

Most of those messages have been cleaned up in RH6.1 & 6.2.   With 5.2 you
should install the errata's and updated for 2.2 kernel use and most all of
those messages will go away.

JJ
