One problem with that advice: the TGA only supports 8bpp (-E1 or
Multia) or 24bpp (-E2 or -E3).  The -E3 should be capable of
running 1024x768 at 24bpp without problems.

> Nik Zapantis wrote:
> > I've installed 6.2 on a AS 200 system, with a ZLX-E3 (TGA 24-bit) card.
> > I cannot setup X to accept this card. I thought 6.2 was supposed to have
> > support for the 24-bit TGA card.
> > Xconfigurator sees the card, I select the appropriate monitor (an Optiquest
> > Q71-2),
> > since Probe cannot configure it, I select the 24-bit 1024x768 mode and no
> > clockchip.
> > When I startx, I get the message that the bpp mode is not supported.

> > what am I missing?

Things to check:

  * You should be running XF86_TGA

  * The screen section of the XF86Config should contain the
    relevant lines (Driver, DefaultColorDepth, Depth) from the
    following:

Section "Screen"
    Driver "accel"
    Device "TGA"
    Monitor "MAG MX15F"
    DefaultColorDepth 24
    Subsection "Display"
        Depth 24
        Modes "1024x768"
    EndSubsection
EndSection



