Alex Rhomberg wrote:
> 
> The description from Compaq seems to indicate that you could use
> 
> #if defined(__DECC_VER) || defined(__DECCXX_VER)
> 
> #endif
> 
> To determine the compiler at compile time. No command lines needed
> 
> - Alex

Right.

No guarantees on code quality/style, but if you wanted to printf
the name of the compiler and its version, handing Compaq C/C++
and gcc/g++, one way might be as follows:

%cat ver.c
#if defined(__DECC_VER) || defined(__DECCXX_VER)
#    define VERletnum(x) (((x)/10000) % 10)
#    define VERletter(x) (VERletnum(x) == 9 ? 'V' \
                      : VERletnum(x) == 6 ? 'T' \
                      : 'X' )
#    define VERmajor(x) ((x)/10000000)
#    define VERminor(x) (((x)/100000) %100)
#    define VERedit(x)  ((x) % 10000)
#    if defined(__DECC_VER)
#        define VERname "Compaq C"
#        define VERnum __DECC_VER
#    else
#        define VERname "Compaq C++"
#        define VERnum __DECCXX_VER
#    endif
#    define VERPRINT() printf("%s %c%d.%d-%03d\n", \
                            VERname, VERletter(VERnum), \
                            VERmajor(VERnum), VERminor(VERnum), \
                            VERedit(VERnum))
#elif defined(__GNUC__)
#    ifdef __cplusplus
#        define VERname "g++"
#    else
#        define VERname "gcc"
#    endif
#    define VERPRINT() printf("%s %d.%d\n", VERname, \
                              __GNUC__, __GNUC_MINOR__)
#else
#    define VERPRINT() printf("UNKNOWN compiler\n")
#endif

#include <stdio.h>
int main(void)
{
    VERPRINT();
    return 0;
}

% gcc ver.c
% ./a.out
gcc 2.90
% g++ ver.c
% ./a.out
g++ 2.90
% ccc ver.c
% ./a.out
Compaq C V6.2-002
% cxx -x cxx ver.c
This beta test software will expire on April 15, 2000.
Please contact Compaq to receive a more recent version.
% ./a.out
Compaq C++ T6.3-003

Of course, if you were going to provide the version of the
compiler for the purpose of reporting a problem, you would
want to invoke the Compaq compilers with the -V option,
or the GNU compilers with the --version option.

   - Compaq C/C++ Team



