Hi,

if you've already got (and want to keep) NT, then it's a whole lot
easier.

All you need to do is put milo(udb-noname), linload.exe and a kernel
(generic.gz, not .img) in the root directory of your 'system'
partition (the
FAT partition that currently contains your osloader).

Don't bother trying to build milo, you're making unnecessary work for
yourself (I know, been there, done that, now cured).

Then make your 'root' floppy (ramdisk.img), and leave it in the drive.

Then from the ARC console, create a new boot entry for your milo,
using the instructions on your RedHat CD (they're there somewhere).
I'm not sure off the top of my head, but basically copy your existing
NT
entry, then change the <blah>\osloader entry to \linload.exe, then
change the osloadfilename to milo, and the directory to \.

Then boot your milo. From there you can boot the floppy root image,
which should then take you through the install process. Now here
I get stuck, because it's been soooo long since I did it, but I'm sure
the online help in milo will sort you out.

Unfortunately, my Multia is my Internet connection, so booting it is
not practical right now for me to check.

I'm sure someone else will correct the small errors that are almost
