This isn't what you requested specifically, but here goes...

if you have 3 commands, one to execute, one for when the first
one fails and one for when the first one works, here's how to do
it in /bin/sh

command && do_when_worked || do_when_fails

So, if you have three scripts, one that tries to establish ppp
connection, one for starting up lynx and one for when it fails,
you can use the above syntax for that.

Make sure that the first script returns 0 when it works and some
non-zero value when it doesn't, because that's what the && and ||
work from.

If you already knew all of this, maybe someone else will get some
benefit from it.

Feel free to post your scripts, I'm sure that other people will
have this issue in the future.

Regards,

Tony Hammitt



