Hello,


Compaq has released the long awaited C++ compiler for linux/alpha.
Fortunately, the provided rpm packages can be used succesfully with Debian.

For the release announcement, see:
http://www.unix.digital.com/linux/compaq_cxx/

To use it with Debian/woody, you need to 
convert these RPMs with alien:

libots
cpml
ccc
cxx

I don't think you do not have to install compaqs binutils, as the current
woody binutils is up to date.

For gcc emulation, use -stdgnu (and not '-std gnu' as stated in docs)

I have one remaining problem though:
Now I have a gnu and a compaq compiler installed, and I would like
to print runtime msgs in my app, stating the compiler that was used.

Unfortunately, compaqs compiler seems to come without a
/usr/lib/compaq/ccc-6.2.9.002-2/alpha-linux/bin/cpp,
so gnu's cpp is used, which expands the __VERSION__ macro to
gcc's version string, and not ccc's version string.

   Bram


